From: Adn Elkawass <elkawasadn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aon-generate: drop O_DIRECT for small writes

aon-generate.sh writes ELF header fields using dd with bs=1.
O_DIRECT requires the I/O buffer, offset, and length to satisfy the
underlying filesystem alignment requirements, so these byte-granularity
writes can fail with EINVAL and leave the generated ELF incomplete.

Drop oflag=direct and use normal buffered writes for these small writes.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet submitted upstream]
Signed-off-by: Adn Elkawass <elkawasadn@gmail.com>
---
 aon-generate.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aon-generate.sh b/aon-generate.sh
--- a/aon-generate.sh
+++ b/aon-generate.sh
@@ -41 +41 @@
-	dd of="$outputFile" oflag=direct conv=notrunc bs=1 seek="$1" status=none
+	dd of="$outputFile" conv=notrunc bs=1 seek="$1" status=none
